    {
      "id": "s06",
      "index": 5,
      "text": "Oil Gallery (Main) Head 23. Oil Passage from Filter 11. \u041e\u0438 Passage to Oil 18. Oil Gallery to Camshaft to Oil Cooler Fig. 2 - Cylinder Block (6V Cast tron Cylinder Block Shown) Each cylinder liner is retained in the block by a flange block bore. An individual compression gasket is used at its upper end, which seats in the counterbore in the at each cylinder. When the cylinder head is installed, the gaskets and seal rings compress sufficiently to form a tight metal- to-metal contact between the head and the block. The In-Line cylinder blocks were revised at the idler gear hub mounting pads, to increase the rigidity of the",
